# The caddy image builds with client/ as its build context (see
# deployment/caddy/Dockerfile), so this file — not the repo-root .dockerignore —
# governs what is sent to the daemon. Keep node_modules/.turbo out of the
# context so the host-resolved tree never lands over `pnpm install`.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.turbo
**/.turbo
dist
**/dist
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
coverage
**/coverage
*.log
.DS_Store
.git

# NOTE: pnpm-lock.yaml and pnpm-workspace.yaml are COPYed explicitly by the
# Dockerfile — never ignore them. routeTree.gen.ts is regenerated during the
# build but kept available.
